From 040d93030ee3bd61ca9140c1af5ac6c99bc4a454 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: evilcomputer12 <martinrobotika@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:33:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] xodus-service: Report identity claims with
 TokenAndSignatureResponse.

Success replies now carry the Xuid, gamertags, age group and user hash of
the user the XSTS token was issued for. The title-bound and user-only paths
are split into title_xsts (session + per-relying-party token from the shared
state) and user_only_xsts (ephemeral cache + MSA exchange) that return the
token and its claims, with the HRESULT mapping carried by TokenError, so a
second message type can reuse them. The Authorization value is now built from
the parsed claims instead of xal's panicking accessor: a token without a user
hash is reported as E_FAIL.

First tests of the service crate: the frame encoding, and the signed-out and
malformed-request replies of parse_message, which need neither keychain nor
network.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
